      "value": "@{60c0e22718009c104862d5bc|full_name}: You're mostly right. But it's not a drop that's the main cause. It's the route change to and from VRChat.\n\nExample:\n\nOriginal Route\n\n127.0.0.1\n\n192.168.1.12\n\n192.168.0.1\n\nSome ISP internet IP\n\nISP route XX1\n\nVRC route XX1\n\nVRC\n\nNew route\n\n127.0.0.1\n\n192.168.1.12\n\n192.168.0.1\n\nSome ISP internet IP\n\nISP route XX2 (Timed out here)\n\nVRC route XX1\n\nVRC\n\n* No personal information was given above. This is all local and default information",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
