  "details": "Since 2 months I am constantly getting kicked without apparent reasons.\nI noticed I am able to play for hours without issues, but sometimes, I can only play for 1-2 min. To describe the issue, after joining a lobby, I can see people moving and talking and they can see and hear me as well, then suddenly people around me stop moving and talking, everyone just freeze. My ping is also stuck at its last state, usually around 60. On their side, they see me freezing like if I crashed. On my side I can still walk around frozen people and most of the game menu isn't responding anymore. However, while I am \"timing out\", recently changed avatars are still downloading and loading normally, which seams to indicate that my connection is still fine with some parts of the game. After 1-2 minutes, I get this error message \"Your connection to VRChat timed out\". Pressing \"Okay\" reloads the instance and I can play for another 2 min until I enters in this \"timing out\" state and kicked again and again. If the world is really big, this issue can also happen during the downloading menu and I am getting instantly kicked as soon as the download is finished. If I restart the game then the issue is less likely to happen and I often can play normally again, but changing world will more likely trigger this issue. Could you please look into this issue? Thank you\n\nEdit: I did more tests. its more random than I thought. The issue come and go away randomly. I would say 1-10 times in a row until the issue go away by itself or by restarting the game. But there is a common pattern : it is always happening within the first 2 minute after changing/joining a world. It is like there is a check, if the check pass, then I can enter and stay in the world without the described issue as long as I want, but if for some reason the check fails then the game kick me out even if everything is ok.\n\nOutput Log:\n\nhttps://dl.dropbox.com/s/ifrx5m66tepmtvb/output_log_18-47-54.txt\n\nIssue happening at line 985.",
